{
 "c": "C3",
 "rev": true,
 "lead": "Living plants and cultures a person keeps or grows, from houseplants, aroids, orchids, succulents and garden plants to fruit trees, seeds and bulbs, bonsai, cut flowers and mushroom, ferment and brewing cultures, organised genus → species → registered cultivar or strain → form, with breeders and craft traditions in the registers.",
 "ax": "What is the plant or culture for, and how is it sold: as seed or bulb, trained as bonsai, cut for a vase, kept indoors, grown in the garden, grown for food, or kept as a living culture?",
 "key": [
  "1. Is it seed, a bulb, corm, tuber or an unrooted cutting sold to plant? → Seeds, bulbs & cuttings",
  "2. Is it a living culture for mushrooms, a ferment, brewing or algae? → Mushrooms & living cultures",
  "3. Is it a tree trained in a shallow pot, or a moss-ball or accent planting shown with one? → Bonsai",
  "4. Is it sold cut: stems, an arrangement, a wreath or a Christmas tree? → Cut flowers & Christmas trees",
  "5. Does it trap and digest animals? → Carnivorous plants",
  "6. Is it an orchid? → Orchids",
  "7. Is it a cactus or another water-storing succulent? → Succulents & cacti",
  "8. Is it a member of the arum family, such as monstera, philodendron or peace lily? → Aroids",
  "9. Is it grown for food: fruit, nuts, herbs or vegetables? → Grow your own",
  "10. Is it kept indoors for leaf, flower or hanging display? → Houseplants",
  "11. Is it an ornamental grown outdoors: rose, shrub, tree, climber, perennial, bedding, pond plant or lawn? → Garden plants",
  "<i>Precedence: an aroid sold as a houseplant is an aroid (step 8) before a houseplant (step 10); a lemon tree kept in a pot is Grow your own (step 9); a seed packet of any plant is step 1.</i>"
 ],
 "b": [],
 "depts": [
  {
   "n": "Aroids",
   "mode": "variety",
   "note": "One department for the arum family, everyday houseplants and collector species alike; genus is the kind, species and named cultivars are archetypes.",
   "b": [
    {
     "m": "True to name and identity",
     "v": "species/cultivar verified > trade name",
     "w": "Aroid trade names are often unresolved; collectors prize correct identity."
    },
    {
     "m": "Variegation stability",
     "v": "stable > unstable",
     "w": "Variegated collector aroids are priced on it."
    },
    {
     "m": "Plant form at sale",
     "v": "established plant > rooted cutting > node > tissue-culture plantlet",
     "w": "How collector aroids are offered and priced."
    }
   ],
   "t": "Plants of the arum family kept for leaves or spathes, whether climbing, upright or tuberous; a food taro → J4, an aquarium aroid → B10, a non-arum houseplant → Houseplants.",
   "ax": "Does it climb or trail on a stem, grow upright from a crown, or die back to a tuber or rhizome?",
   "s": [
    {
     "n": "Climbing & trailing aroids",
     "t": "Aroids that climb or trail on aerial stems, such as monstera and pothos; an upright aroid → Upright aroids.",
